<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#nutmeg">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nutmeg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nutmeg is a spice obtained from the seed of a tree native to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banda-islands">Banda Islands</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a> of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. It was among the most valuable commodities of the early modern spice trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> profited from the spice trade in the sixteenth century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> later enforced a monopoly through violence, including the near-extermination of the Banda Islanders in 1621.</p></div>
